amentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Florida remains a Republican-leaning state at the presidential level, and with the incumbent term-limited, both parties head toward open nominating contests. Early attention centers on Republicans such as Marco Rubio, JD Vance, and Ron DeSantis, while Pete Buttigieg has headlined Florida Democratic events. No general-election polls or expert ratings exist yet, so the rating rests on the state's partisan lean, which favors Republicans by mid-single digits.\n\nThe strongest counterweight is Democratic momentum from 2026, when a surprisingly close governor's race and other results suggested Florida is more competitive than recent presidential results implied. Midterm energy, though, has not reliably carried into presidential years in Florida, where Republican turnout advantages have persisted. The race stays in the Republican-lean column with unusually wide uncertainty until nominees are chosen and real polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2832, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3401, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3574, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3674, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3674, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3461, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3181, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3285, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3519, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3384, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3288, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3332, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3286, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "